  "slug": "expanding-glycomics-0644",
  "summary": "NAR database-issue updates (CIViC, DGIdb, FusionGDB, VEuPathDB, CNCB-NGDC) appear alongside new APIs and storage formats for cohort-scale genomic data.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is maturation of community genomic resources toward machine-accessible, reproducible infrastructure. Several knowledgebase updates emphasise interoperability: DGIdb adds Python/R clients, Docker images and versioned releases; CIViC introduces Feature entities, Molecular Profiles, AI-guided curation and ClinVar submission; VEuPathDB reports 2,602 datasets, AI-assisted curation and a PostgreSQL migration. FusionGDB 3.0 integrates RNA-seq and WGS breakpoints for 156K fusion genes and generates personalised fusion protein sequences. CNCB-NGDC adds thirteen resources, and CiliaHub curates over 2,500 ciliary genes with ClinVar and orthology data. Programmatic access extends to project data: pyGENIE wraps AACR GENIE files with TMB and signature analysis, and the IGVF Data Portal exposes knowledge-graph-integrated results via an API including agentic-tool support. On the storage side, pbzarr proposes Zarr for per-base data across thousands of samples, reported smaller and faster than D4 and bigWig. Met4All packages Infinium methylation analysis as a dockerised Shiny app.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-23"
}
